    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "TheaterEvent",
      "id": "22cbbad268f11889",
      "title": "Louis C.K.",
      "description": "25 - 26 Φεβρουαριου Louis C.K. CHRISTMAS THEATER",
      "fullDescription": "The lights go down and the Christmas Theater holds its breath. Two thousand seats, one microphone, and whatever Louis C.K. has decided to say tonight. No warm-up act. No production values beyond a man standing in a spotlight. This is stand-up stripped to its essentials.\n\nLouis C.K. returns to Athens carrying both his reputation and his history. The comedy that made him one of the most influential voices of his generation — the unflinching observations about marriage, parenting, aging, and the absurdities of human existence — now exists alongside everything that happened after. He's addressed it onstage, folded it into the work. The audiences who show up in 2026 know what they're getting: someone who turned his own implosion into material.\n\nThe Christmas Theater crowd for this show represents a particular slice of comedy appreciation. You'll find expats who followed Louis from his American club days, Greeks who discovered him through specials and podcasts, and curious observers who want to see what he does with an Athens audience. The laughter comes in waves — sometimes surprised, sometimes uncomfortable, always engaged with a performer who has never taken the easy path.\n\nThe venue provides the scale this show needs. Purpose-built for performance, the Christmas Theater offers sightlines that work from every seat and acoustics that carry a single voice to the back rows without effort. When Louis lands a punchline, you hear the reaction ripple through two thousand people simultaneously.\n\nIf you need comedy that stays in safe territory, that avoids the complicated parts of its performer's biography, this isn't your show. Louis C.K. has built his late-career sets around the premise that nothing is off-limits — including himself. But if you want to see one of the most influential stand-ups of his generation working without a net, testing material on an audience that came specifically to see what he'd do — you end up here.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Wednesday, February 25, 2026 |\n| **Doors** | 19:30 |\n| **Show** | 21:00 |\n| **Venue** | Christmas Theater, Athens |\n| **Price** | €40-80 depending on seating |\n| **Language** | English |\n\nNo safety net. No apologies. Just a comedian and whatever he's decided to say.",
      "startDate": "2026-02-25T20:00:00+03:00",
      "endDate": null,
